<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19524" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gĕrŭlus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A bearer</i>, <i>carrier</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nae ille alium gerulum (argenti) quaerat sibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 4, 9, 79</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 2, 72</span></i>; Col.
			poët. 10, 310; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Calig. 40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 13</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 575</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">874</span></i>; <i><span class="en">976</span></i>; Schol. <i><span class="en">Juv. 6,
			477</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>One who does</i> something, <i>a
			doer</i>: gerulus <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ πράττων, ὁ
			πρακτήρ</span>, Gloss. Philox.; cf. gerulifigulus.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
